        {
          "id": 1231979535,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I'm fine with merging this as is if it solves an issue on Windows. Maybe we can remove the `if (false && ...)` hack from `ws_assert()` too while at it.\n\nThis was an issue only with Clang and [Wused-but-marked-unused](https://clang.llvm.org/docs/DiagnosticsReference.html#wused-but-marked-unused) if I remember correctly but that warning is not currently used and it is annoying and pedantic anyway to have always enabled IMO, for exactly this reason.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2639362,
            "username": "jvalverde",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "João Valverde",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
